1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,478
One worn part can stop a favorite routine.

2
00:00:03,598 --> 00:00:09,684
Useful electronics sit in drawers because
no one knows what to do with them.

3
00:00:09,804 --> 00:00:12,847
Orphan Parts Lens starts with two
questions.

4
00:00:12,967 --> 00:00:16,880
What do you have, and what do you want?

5
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:21,621
This older Hamilton Beach drink mixer
makes frappé coffee.

6
00:00:21,741 --> 00:00:23,794
Its agitator is worn.

7
00:00:23,914 --> 00:00:31,615
The rod has no model number, so the app
asks which device it came from.

8
00:00:31,735 --> 00:00:35,329
The label under the base answers that.

9
00:00:35,449 --> 00:00:40,583
Search the web looks first for the maker's
own part.

10
00:00:40,703 --> 00:00:47,377
It keeps only pages the search returned,
each a listing with its link.

11
00:00:47,497 --> 00:00:53,145
Check fit turns every unknown into a
question for the seller.

12
00:00:53,265 --> 00:00:58,399
Decide weighs fixing, reusing or selling
against the owner's skills.

13
00:00:58,519 --> 00:01:01,086
It calls the fix hard.

14
00:01:01,206 --> 00:01:07,880
But with the maker's part found, the owner
keeps it and fixes it.

15
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:11,421
The same approach works for unused
electronics.

16
00:01:11,541 --> 00:01:17,405
Laptops, monitors and parts go into the
inventory, beside a skills profile.

17
00:01:17,525 --> 00:01:23,878
The preferences say what the build is for
and what it can cost.

18
00:01:23,998 --> 00:01:28,885
Muse Spark proposes projects from what is
in the inventory.

19
00:01:29,005 --> 00:01:32,914
The rules keep only what the inventory
backs.

20
00:01:33,034 --> 00:01:37,432
The arcade that was asked for isn't among
them.

21
00:01:37,552 --> 00:01:43,905
So the homework workstation is selected,
and its items are committed to it.

22
00:01:44,025 --> 00:01:49,400
Draw it shows how it could look, marked as
a drawing.

23
00:01:49,520 --> 00:01:54,896
What is missing becomes a Marketplace
search that the owner runs.

24
00:01:55,016 --> 00:02:00,880
The build pack collects the items, the
steps, and the safety notes.

25
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:03,313
Next, a plan that adapts.

26
00:02:03,433 --> 00:02:08,522
A connection diagram, and a different
display that re-plans the build.

27
00:02:08,642 --> 00:02:11,880
These are concept previews, not built yet.

28
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:18,063
On the phone, photos and a spoken note go
into the same inventory.

29
00:02:18,183 --> 00:02:24,245
The models are Muse Spark, SAM 3.1, Muse
Voice Transcribe and Muse Image.

30
00:02:24,365 --> 00:02:28,563
They do the reading, the searching and the
drawing.

31
00:02:28,683 --> 00:02:32,880
Anyone can try it on the owner's own
photos.

32
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:35,556
Orphan Parts Lens.

33
00:02:35,676 --> 00:02:37,380
Find replacements.

34
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:39,204
Discover reuse.

35
00:02:39,324 --> 00:02:41,880
Build something useful.

